SPEECH -- CVSD tandem on the 8 kHz line, with far idle tones and notches

  Path: encode → decode (near) → [8 kHz] → tones? → notches? → bandlimit
  → encode → decode (far).
  segSNR against a *notched* clean path so the score is the whistle,
  not the spectral holes the notches cut in the reference.

  plain path vs itself:     segSNR  35.0 dB
  notched vs plain:         segSNR   9.6 dB (spectral holes — not a fault)
  notched vs notched:       segSNR  35.0 dB

  condition                                 segSNR dB  W residue dB
  tones + leak, no notches                        8.4          -0.7
  tones + leak + notches                         35.0         -94.7
  tones + notches + SNR 20                       17.5         -94.7
  tones + notches + SNR 10                       10.0         -94.7
  notches only (no tones)                        35.0         -94.7

  Residue is mean W-bin level re a clean dual tone; notches should
  drive it deep negative.  segSNR uses the notched clean path as ref
  whenever notches are on, so a dead whistle reads near the ceiling.

  [speech: 24.4 s]

